# Pairs with CausalOrder. A silo latches the floor on its own upgrade instead of waiting for the
# cluster manifest to show every active silo capable, so a partition on an old-build silo publishes a
# floor it cannot enforce.
MODULE: CausalOrderSiloOpensItsOwnGate
TARGET: CausalOrder
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a silo enables the floor on its own upgrade, while another silo still runs the old build
PERTURBS: Upgrade

--- FIND
    /\ ~capable[p] /\ capable' = [capable EXCEPT ![p] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<aAuth, aCom, alog, floor, pub, spart, floorOn>> /\ UNCHANGED Wire /\ UNCHANGED Rcv
--- REPLACE
    /\ ~capable[p] /\ capable' = [capable EXCEPT ![p] = TRUE]
    \* MUTATION: the silo's own upgrade opens the gate.
    /\ floorOn' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<aAuth, aCom, alog, floor, pub, spart>> /\ UNCHANGED Wire /\ UNCHANGED Rcv
--- END
